**Effective Date:** 19 October 2026

## 1. Definitions

For the purposes of this Notice, the following definitions apply:

* **"EuroLoot"** means the EuroLoot business, its owner, and any associated products, services, platforms, or projects operated under the EuroLoot name, subject to the applicable ownership of each asset.
* **"EuroLoot Website"** means the website operated under the EuroLoot name, including its pages, interfaces, web applications, features, visual components, and associated online properties.
* **"Source Code"** means the human-readable and machine-readable code and related implementation materials used to develop, generate, maintain, or operate the EuroLoot Website, including HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript, scripts, configuration files, build files, and other original software components.
* **"Materials"** means the original text, graphics, illustrations, designs, logos, branding, layouts, visual assets, documentation, and other copyrightable content associated with the EuroLoot Website.
* **"Intellectual Property"** means the copyright, design rights, trademarks, and other intellectual property rights owned by or lawfully licensed to the relevant rights holder in connection with EuroLoot.
* **"Rights Holder"** means Colm Lenehan or another person or legal entity that owns or is legally entitled to enforce the relevant rights in a particular work, asset, or component.
* **"You"** and **"Your"** mean any individual, organisation, company, or other entity accessing, viewing, using, copying, or otherwise interacting with the EuroLoot Website, its Source Code, or its Materials.

## 2. Ownership and Reservation of Rights

Unless expressly identified otherwise, the original works comprising the EuroLoot Website and its associated Materials are protected by applicable intellectual property laws.

Copyright in original works created by Colm Lenehan for EuroLoot is owned by Colm Lenehan, subject to any applicable agreements, assignments, third-party rights, and statutory exceptions.

The relevant Rights Holder retains all rights, title, and interest in and to the Intellectual Property owned by that Rights Holder. Nothing in this Notice transfers ownership of any Intellectual Property to You.

Except where expressly permitted by applicable law or authorised in writing by the relevant Rights Holder, no licence, permission, or other right is granted to You to reproduce, modify, adapt, distribute, publish, commercialise, sublicense, or otherwise exploit protected works from the EuroLoot Website.

Access to, viewing of, or interaction with the EuroLoot Website does not, by itself, grant a licence to use its underlying Source Code, original designs, branding, or other protected Materials for purposes beyond those permitted by law.

All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

## 3. Restrictions on Use

Subject to applicable law, You must not, without the prior written permission of the relevant Rights Holder:

* **Copy or redistribute protected works:** Reproduce, republish, distribute, sell, sublicense, lease, or commercially exploit the EuroLoot Website, its Source Code, or its original Materials, in whole or in part.
* **Create derivative works:** Modify, adapt, translate, reconstruct, or create derivative works from protected Source Code, designs, graphics, or other Materials, except where such activity is permitted by law or an applicable licence.
* **Republish the website:** Mirror, clone, reproduce, or host substantial portions of the EuroLoot Website or its protected Materials on another website, application, platform, or service.
* **Misrepresent affiliation:** Use EuroLoot's name, logos, branding, or other identifying Materials in a manner that falsely suggests sponsorship, endorsement, ownership, partnership, or official affiliation.
* **Commercialise protected Materials:** Incorporate protected EuroLoot Materials into a competing product or service, commercial offering, template, or distribution package without the required authorisation.
* **Circumvent technical protections:** Bypass, disable, or interfere with technical access controls or security measures protecting the EuroLoot Website, where such conduct is unlawful or otherwise prohibited by applicable terms or law.
* **Misuse access:** Use unauthorised methods to obtain restricted Source Code, credentials, confidential information, or other materials that You are not entitled to access.
* **Misuse Materials for automated systems:** Use protected Materials or Source Code for machine learning, generative artificial intelligence, dataset creation, or model training where such use requires permission and no applicable licence, legal exception, or other lawful basis permits it.

Nothing in this section prohibits conduct that is expressly authorised by an applicable open-source or third-party licence, permitted by applicable law, or otherwise authorised by the relevant Rights Holder.

## 4. Source Code and Repository Access

The availability of Source Code in a public code repository, deployment platform, browser, or other publicly accessible location does not, by itself, mean that the Source Code is licensed for unrestricted reuse.

Unless an applicable licence or written permission provides otherwise, You must not assume that public availability authorises You to copy, modify, redistribute, or commercially exploit the EuroLoot Website or its Source Code.

Certain website components may necessarily be transmitted to Your browser or made available through publicly accessible technical resources. This does not automatically grant permission to reproduce or republish those components beyond the scope permitted by law.

Where a specific repository, dependency, library, asset, or other component is subject to a separate licence, that licence governs the rights it grants in that component. Nothing in this Notice overrides rights expressly granted under a valid third-party licence.

## 5. Third-Party Materials and Exclusions

EuroLoot may use or reference software libraries, frameworks, fonts, images, APIs, trademarks, services, and other materials owned by third parties.

Such materials remain subject to their respective owners' rights and applicable licence terms. They are not automatically owned by Colm Lenehan or EuroLoot merely because they are incorporated into, displayed on, or used by the EuroLoot Website.

Similarly, general ideas, methods, functionality, programming concepts, and other subject matter that is not protected by copyright are not claimed as exclusive property merely by virtue of this Notice.

Nothing in this Notice is intended to assert ownership over materials that the Rights Holder does not own or have the legal authority to control.

## 6. Trademarks and Branding

The EuroLoot name, logo, slogans, visual identity, and other brand identifiers may be protected by applicable trademark, copyright, design, or other intellectual property laws, to the extent such protection applies.

Unless expressly authorised, You must not use EuroLoot branding in a manner that infringes applicable rights, misleads the public, or falsely implies an official relationship with EuroLoot.

Any trademark rights asserted under this Notice are limited to rights actually owned by or lawfully available to the relevant Rights Holder. This Notice does not, by itself, establish that a trademark has been registered.

## 7. Enforcement and Available Remedies

The relevant Rights Holder reserves the right to take appropriate action in response to actual or threatened infringement of rights protected by applicable law.

Depending on the circumstances and the applicable legal framework, available remedies may include:

* Requests to cease or remove infringing material.
* Applications for interim or permanent injunctive relief where legally available.
* Claims for damages, compensation, or other financial remedies where legally available.
* Recovery of legal costs where recoverable under applicable law.
* Requests for the removal or disabling of infringing material through relevant hosting providers, platforms, or other appropriate channels.
* Referral to competent authorities where the conduct may constitute an offence under applicable law.

The availability, scope, and conditions of any remedy depend on the facts of the matter and the applicable law. Nothing in this Notice guarantees a particular outcome or creates a remedy that would not otherwise be available.

## 8. No Waiver

Failure or delay by the relevant Rights Holder to exercise a right or remedy does not, by itself, constitute a waiver of that right or remedy.

Any waiver must be interpreted in accordance with its terms and applicable law. A permission granted for one purpose, work, or period does not automatically constitute permission for other purposes, works, or periods.

The relevant Rights Holder reserves all rights and remedies available under applicable law.

## 9. Severability

If any provision of this Notice is found to be invalid, unlawful, or unenforceable, that provision shall be limited or interpreted to the minimum extent necessary to address the issue, where legally permissible.

The remaining provisions shall continue to apply to the extent that they remain valid and enforceable.

## 10. Governing Law and Jurisdiction

Subject to mandatory provisions of applicable law, this Notice shall be interpreted in accordance with the laws of Ireland.

Any dispute concerning this Notice shall be subject to the jurisdiction of the competent courts of Ireland, to the extent that such jurisdiction is legally applicable.

Nothing in this section excludes or limits any mandatory rights, protections, or jurisdictional rules that apply under European Union law or other applicable law.

## 11. Requests for Permission and Licensing

Requests to reproduce, adapt, distribute, commercialise, or otherwise use protected EuroLoot Materials beyond what is permitted by law should be submitted to the relevant Rights Holder in writing.

Requests should identify:

* The individual or organisation requesting permission.
* The specific Material or Source Code concerned.
* The intended purpose and scope of the proposed use.
* Whether the proposed use is commercial or non-commercial.
* The expected distribution, publication, or deployment arrangements.

Permission is granted only to the extent expressly authorised by the relevant Rights Holder or an authorised representative. Any licence should specify its scope, duration, permitted uses, and applicable conditions.

Contact details for permissions should be published through an official EuroLoot contact channel.

## 12. Amendments to This Notice

The relevant Rights Holder may update this Notice to reflect changes to the EuroLoot Website, its ownership arrangements, applicable licences, or relevant legal requirements.

The effective date displayed at the beginning of this Notice identifies the date of the current version. A revised version should include an updated effective date.

An amendment to this Notice does not retroactively remove rights already granted under a valid licence or agreement, except where permitted by its terms and applicable law.

## 13. Contact

For copyright, intellectual property, licensing, or permissions enquiries, please use the official EuroLoot contact channel published on the EuroLoot Website.

For formal legal correspondence, please identify the relevant work, the rights concerned, and the nature of the enquiry.

